## PART 6: THE LEGAL DISTINCTION - POSSESSION/CREATION vs. ILLEGAL USE

| Activity | Legal Status | Why |
|----------|-------------|-----|
| **Building a C2 framework** | ✅ LEGAL | DOJ policy protects good-faith research [citation:2][citation:5] |
| **Possessing malware samples** | ✅ LEGAL | Van Buren: authorization determines legality, not policy [citation:3][citation:7] |
| **Creating exploit code** | ✅ LEGAL | Code is speech; research is protected |
| **Running tools in isolated VM** | ✅ LEGAL | You own the system; no unauthorized access |
| **Testing on authorized systems** | ✅ LEGAL | Written permission = authorization |
| | | |
| **USING tool without permission** | ❌ ILLEGAL | Unauthorized access under CFAA |
| **USING tool with intent to damage** | ❌ ILLEGAL | Mens rea requirement under 18 U.S.C. § 1030(a)(5)(A) |

