## PART 8: WHAT THE CFAA ACTUALLY CRIMINALIZES - 18 U.S.C. § 1030(a)(5)(A)

The elements that must ALL be proven for a violation [citation:3][citation:7]:

| Element | Requirement |
|---------|-------------|
| **Knowingly** | Defendant knew they were transmitting |
| **Caused transmission** | Defendant sent code/command |
| **Intentionally** | Defendant MEANT to cause damage |
| **Caused damage** | Actual damage occurred |
| **Without authorization** | No permission from computer owner |
| **To a protected computer** | Computer used in interstate commerce |

**If you build a tool but never use it to access someone else's computer without permission — NO CRIME.**

**If you build a tool and use it on YOUR OWN computer in an isolated VM — NO CRIME.**

**If you build a tool and use it with permission on an authorized testbed — NO CRIME.**

